genuine Windows only: the UCRT reads an unbuffered stdin two bytes at a time (measured 2026-10-10: after scanf("%d") on a piped '4321\nn * 2', the next OS byte is ' ' — 'n' sits in the backend's FILE), so a piped stdin cannot be shared byte-exactly between the REPL host and its backend process (split arc 1A.5); a console delivers whole lines and is exact, and wine's CRT reads byte by byte (the wine64 lane runs this test)
